-- title:
--   Spreading triviality of K from the local ring to a basic open
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a noetherian commutative ring, $f\colon A\to\operatorname{Spec}S$ a morphism of schemes, $L$ a relative group law on $f$ (a functorial group structure on the sets $\{\varphi:T\to A\mid \varphi\circ f=t\}$ of sections over varying $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}S$, natural in $T$), and assume the bundle `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` for $f$: $f$ is smooth and proper, each fibre $f^{-1}(s)$ is connected, and a relative group law exists. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime of $S$ and $r\in S\setminus\mathfrak p$. Let $C$ be an $S$-algebra and $S_r$-algebra with compatible scalar tower, finite as an $S_r$-module, and let $\mathcal L'$ be an invertible module (locally trivialisable in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible`) on $A_C=A\times_{\operatorname{Spec}S}\operatorname{Spec}C$. Let $C_{\mathfrak p}$ be an $S$- and $C$-algebra, compatibly, which is a localisation of $C$ at the multiplicative set generated by the image of $S\setminus\mathfrak p$, let $\varphi\colon A_{C_{\mathfrak p}}\to A_C$ be a morphism whose composites with the two projections are the first projection of $A_{C_{\mathfrak p}}$ and, respectively, the second projection followed by $\operatorname{Spec}(C\to C_{\mathfrak p})$, and let $L_{\mathfrak p}$ be a relative group law on $A_{C_{\mathfrak p}}\to\operatorname{Spec}C_{\mathfrak p}$ compatible with $L$, in the sense that for all $T$, $t'\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}C_{\mathfrak p}$ and sections $P,Q$, the underlying morphism of $L_{\mathfrak p}.\mathrm{mul}\,t'\,P\,Q$ followed by the projection to $A$ equals the $L$-product of the projected sections. Assume `KernelTrivial` for $\varphi^*\mathcal L'$ with respect to $L_{\mathfrak p}$: for every commutative ring $R$, every $t\colon\operatorname{Spec}R\to\operatorname{Spec}C_{\mathfrak p}$ and every section $x$ of $A_{C_{\mathfrak p}}$ over $t$, if the restriction along $\mathrm{sliceAt}\,x$ of the Mumford bundle of $\varphi^*\mathcal L'$ is, locally on each point of $\operatorname{Spec}R$, isomorphic to the unit module, then $x$ is the identity section. The conclusion is that there exists $g\in S\setminus\mathfrak p$ such that for every $S$- and $C$-algebra $C_g$ with compatible tower which is a localisation of $C$ at the image of the powers of $g$, every morphism $\varphi_g\colon A_{C_g}\to A_C$ satisfying the same two projection identities, and every relative group law $L_g$ on $A_{C_g}\to\operatorname{Spec}C_g$ compatible with $L$ in the same sense, `KernelTrivial` holds for $\varphi_g^*\mathcal L'$ with respect to $L_g$.
--
--   This is a spreading-out step: the statement that the kernel of a line bundle on an abelian scheme is trivial, known over the localisation of a finite algebra $C$ at a prime of the noetherian base, already holds over a localisation of $C$ at the powers of a single element outside that prime. It feeds the corresponding statement for localisations at powers of an element in the good-reduction analysis of Jacobians, via [`GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_not_mem_dvd_forall_isLocalization_powers_kernelTrivial_pullback_of_kernelTrivial_atPrime`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_not_mem_dvd_forall_isLocalization_powers_kernelTrivial_pullback_of_kernelTrivial_atPrime).
